# Tech Stack Checker — core rules

## Layer boundaries

- **`src/core/`** — shared analysis engine; no React, no Commander, no Next.js imports
- **`src/web/`** — UI only; may import `@/src/core`
- **`src/cli/`** — CLI only; may import `@/src/core` and `@/src/web/report` for HTML export
- **`app/`** — Next.js routes; thin handlers that call `src/core`

## Compliance matching order

1. Exact canonical match (`aliases.ts`)
2. Implied companions (`ecosystem.ts`) — suffix `(implied)` in reports
3. Optional LLM for broad allowed entries only when `useAI` is true — suffix `(AI)`

Do not use AI for detection itself; only for unmatched vs broad allowed-list entries.

## CLI exit codes

- `0` — analysis completed (report printed)
- `1` — non-compliant **only** when `--strict` is passed
- `2` — GitHub/config/runtime errors

## Changes checklist

- New manifest file type → update `INDICATOR_FILES` / tree filters in `github.ts` **and** a detector in `detectors.ts`
- New alias → `aliases.ts` only (keep canonical names consistent with detector output)
- User-facing behavior → update `README.md` if limits or flags change

Keep diffs focused; avoid unrelated refactors.
